# Playing the first release, from orbit to a second territory.
#
# `releases/first-release.md` gives the loop in eight steps. This file walks the first five:
# no presence on the planet, land the ark and claim a territory, work the food extractor to
# grow the population, build extractors for metal and energy, then produce a pioneer and
# spread across the planet by land.
#
# Every line is a command. There is no other way for the state to move, so this file is a
# complete account of the game it produces.

# 1 and 2. The ark comes down, and landing *is* the claiming: it takes the ground and
# becomes a garrison, two citizens, and an extractor for food and one for metal.
#
# The mine is what makes the rest possible. An extractor costs a metal, so ground that
# arrived with only a farm could never build a second thing.
land ark 1

# Turn 1. Two citizens and two extractors, which is what a landing leaves. One holds the food,
# one opens the mine.
create labor 1 1
work 1 extractor 1 food
create labor 1 1
work 1 extractor 1 metal
end turn

# Turn 2. Four citizens. The mine pays for two more farms, which is what turns four into twelve.
create labor 1 1
work 1 extractor 1 food
create labor 1 1
work 1 extractor 1 metal
create labor 1 1
build extractor 1 food
create labor 1 1
build extractor 1 food
end turn

# Turn 3. Three farms feed twelve, and the population is limited by hands rather than by food.
create labor 3 1
work 3 extractor 1 food
create labor 1 1
work 1 extractor 1 metal
end turn

# Turn 4. Eight citizens, four spare hands and four metal: two more mines and the first two wells.
create labor 3 1
work 3 extractor 1 food
create labor 1 1
work 1 extractor 1 metal
create labor 1 1
build extractor 1 metal
create labor 1 1
build extractor 1 metal
create labor 1 1
build extractor 1 energy
create labor 1 1
build extractor 1 energy
end turn

# Turn 5. Twelve, and the last well. From here the territory makes twelve of each a turn.
create labor 3 1
work 3 extractor 1 food
create labor 3 1
work 3 extractor 1 metal
create labor 2 1
work 2 extractor 1 energy
create labor 1 1
build extractor 1 energy
end turn

# Turn 6. Everything worked, and nothing left to build. A pioneer costs three metal, six energy
# and two citizens.
create labor 3 1
work 3 extractor 1 food
create labor 3 1
work 3 extractor 1 metal
create labor 3 1
work 3 extractor 1 energy

# 5. The landing site can send a pioneer out.
produce pioneer 1
end turn

# Turn 7. The farms are worked first - a population that gathers nothing this turn starves
# at the end of it, whatever else is going on.
create labor 3 1
work 3 extractor 1 food
create labor 3 1
work 3 extractor 1 metal
create labor 3 1
work 3 extractor 1 energy

# The pioneer crosses into a neighbouring territory. It is not held, so arriving there takes
# it and claims it: force 2 against a force of nature of 1, and the pioneer becomes a
# garrison, two citizens, a farm and a mine.
move pioneer 2

# The new ground feeds itself on the very turn it is claimed.
create labor 1 2
work 1 extractor 2 food
end turn
